[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3677819596","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114238#issuecomment-3677819596","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114238","id":3677819596,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7bNxLM","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-20T13:21:11Z","updated_at":"2025-12-20T13:21:11Z","body":"Maybe that window ID is not registered in the Wayland backend anymore or it was destroyed earlier (closed window, popup dismissed, drag ended, etc.) or the ID exists in input state (`pd`) but Wayland thread hasn’t created or synced it.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3677819596/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3678864659","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114238#issuecomment-3678864659","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114238","id":3678864659,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7bRwUT","user":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-21T14:52:16Z","updated_at":"2025-12-21T14:52:16Z","body":"cc @deralmas ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3678864659/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3678880377","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114238#issuecomment-3678880377","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114238","id":3678880377,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7bR0J5","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-21T15:13:27Z","updated_at":"2025-12-21T15:13:39Z","body":"@rsubtil \nThis maybe intended behavior as this comment here tells us:\n```c++\n    WindowState *ws = nullptr;\n\n\t// NOTE: At least on sway, with wl_pointer version 5 or greater,\n\t// wl_pointer::leave might be emitted with other events (like\n\t// wl_pointer::button) within the same wl_pointer::frame. Because of this, we\n\t// need to account for when the currently pointed window might be invalid\n\t// (third-party or even none) and fall back to the old one.\n\tif (pd.pointed_id != DisplayServer::INVALID_WINDOW_ID) {\n\t\tws = ss->wayland_thread->window_get_state(pd.pointed_id);\n\t\tERR_FAIL_NULL(ws);\nrest of the code here\n```\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp#L1891-L1900","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3678880377/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3679080146","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114238#issuecomment-3679080146","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114238","id":3679080146,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7bSk7S","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-21T16:39:21Z","updated_at":"2025-12-21T16:39:21Z","body":"Hi, thank you for your report! I'll put this in my TODO list and take a look soon. Please note that as the holidays are approaching so I might take longer than usual.\n\n>  This maybe intended behavior as this comment here tells us\n\nI don't think that this is related. The null check happens after we ensured that the pointed id is not an invalid window id, so the underlying window probably got destroyed.\n\nThe weird thing is that we ensure to handle any leftover event before doing that.\n\n@Unknown977 could you please attach a debug log?\n\n```sh\nWAYLAND_DEBUG=1 path/to/godot --verbose 2>&1 | tee wayland.log\n```\n\nNote that this is a Wayland protocol dump and will include any input to the editor/game.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3679080146/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3679083130","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114238#issuecomment-3679083130","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114238","id":3679083130,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7bSlp6","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-21T16:44:02Z","updated_at":"2025-12-21T16:44:02Z","body":"> I don't think that this is related. The null check happens after we ensured that the pointed id is not an invalid window id, so the underlying window probably got destroyed.\n\nOkay, seems that I may have misunderstood 😅 \n\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3679083130/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3982645395","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114238#issuecomment-3982645395","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114238","id":3982645395,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7tYliT","user":{"login":"Leaaep","id":107401117,"node_id":"U_kgDOBmbPnQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/107401117?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leaaep","html_url":"https://github.com/Leaaep","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leaaep/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leaaep/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leaaep/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leaaep/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leaaep/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leaaep/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leaaep/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leaaep/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Leaaep/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-02T07:34:35Z","updated_at":"2026-03-02T07:34:35Z","body":"Hi I got the same issue with the error: `ERROR: platform/linuxbsd/wayland/wayland_thread.cpp:1900 - Parameter \"ws\" is null.` same DE (Cosmic DE on wayland) but on Pop!_Os instead of Arch. I ran the command:\n> WAYLAND_DEBUG=1 path/to/godot --verbose 2>&1 | tee wayland.log\n\nAnd can provide the logs.\n\n[wayland.log](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/25676331/wayland.log)\n\nHope that helps!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3982645395/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4171255643","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114238#issuecomment-4171255643","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114238","id":4171255643,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74oE9b","user":{"login":"deralmas","id":31065808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMDY1ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31065808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas","html_url":"https://github.com/deralmas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/deralmas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-01T16:22:51Z","updated_at":"2026-04-01T16:22:51Z","body":"Hi, I finally gave a look at the protocol dump and I think the issue stems from the fact that COSMIC doesn't emit a pointer leave event when a window is destroyed.\n\nGenerally the code trusts that a valid ID should point to a valid window. Since it never gets cleared up by a leave event, we try to get the window and error out.\n\nI'll see how to make the code sturdier (or at the very least less chatty) but at the same time I think that there might be a compositor bug.\n\nThe [`wl_pointer::leave`](https://wayland.app/protocols/wayland#wl_pointer:event:leave) documentation says:\n\n> The leave notification is sent before the enter notification for the new focus.\n\nTo me this seems to imply that all `enter` events must be preceded by a `leave` event.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4171255643/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]